coppice, the Rust port (harness/coppice-rs)
Copyright the openDaisugi contributors.

It is part of openDaisugi and is MIT licensed. It builds on these crates
from crates.io, each used under one of the licences it offers:

  serde, serde_core MIT OR Apache-2.0
  serde_json       MIT OR Apache-2.0 (with itoa, MIT OR Apache-2.0; memchr,
                   Unlicense OR MIT; zmij, MIT)
  libc             MIT OR Apache-2.0
  toml             MIT OR Apache-2.0 (with toml_edit, toml_datetime and
                   serde_spanned, MIT OR Apache-2.0; winnow, MIT; indexmap,
                   hashbrown and equivalent, Apache-2.0 OR MIT)
  regex            MIT OR Apache-2.0 (with regex-automata and regex-syntax,
                   MIT OR Apache-2.0)
  rustls           Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT (the phone server's TLS)
  ring             Apache-2.0 AND ISC (rustls's crypto and the local CA's
                   keys; carries C and assembly code, compiled by its build
                   script, with getrandom, once_cell and cfg-if, MIT OR
                   Apache-2.0)
  rustls-pki-types MIT OR Apache-2.0
  rustls-webpki    ISC
  untrusted        ISC
  subtle           BSD-3-Clause
  zeroize          Apache-2.0 OR MIT

The crates that only run at build time (serde_derive, proc-macro2, quote,
syn, unicode-ident, cc, shlex, find-msvc-tools) are not in the binary.
The Rust standard library (MIT OR Apache-2.0, used under Apache-2.0,
Copyright the Rust Project Developers) is linked into the binary. The
exact crate versions are in harness/coppice-rs/Cargo.lock, and
harness/coppice-rs/PINS.md says why each one is there.

The parts below are the same as the Go coppice's, or ported from it, so
their notices follow as the Go coppice's NOTICE gives them.

